shadcn output lands here — VENDORED SOURCE we own and edit, not a dependency. There is no upstream
version, no lockfile entry for a component, and no update path.

`shadcn add --overwrite` replaces a file wholesale and discards every local edit, so run
`shadcn add --diff <component>` before any re-add.

THE BASE IS NOT SELECTED BY A FLAG AT THE PINNED VERSION, and the sentence that used to sit here
claimed it was. shadcn 4.16.1 (the pin) has no `-b`/`--base` option at all — `shadcn add -b radix`
exits 1 with `error: unknown option '-b'` — and `base` is not a key its `components.json` schema
accepts either. What actually decides the base is the STYLE the CLI resolves: it detects Tailwind v4
and rewrites style `new-york` to `new-york-v4`, whose registry items declare the unified `radix-ui`
package (already a dependency at an exact pin) rather than the per-primitive `@radix-ui/react-*`
packages the legacy `new-york` items use. The ten components here were taken from that resolved
registry and `shadcn add <component> --diff` reports "No changes." for every one of them.
Re-introduce a `-b` flag or a `base` key only together with a CLI version whose `--help` lists it;
until then it is a claim nothing enforces.

Nothing in this directory crosses into apps/widget: Radix is React-only, and cva + tailwind-merge +
lucide-react are runtime dependencies that would eat the widget's 30 kB brotli budget.
